<div class="page">
  <h1 class="page-title">Philosophy</h1>
  <p class="page-subtitle">How I think about building software, leading teams, and solving problems that matter.</p>

  <article style="margin-bottom: 36px;">
    <h2 style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--dusk-blue); margin-bottom: 8px;">Simplicity Is Leverage</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite);">The best systems I've worked on are easy to explain. Not because they're trivial, but because they're intentional. Complexity is not strength. Simplicity, earned through understanding, is.</p>
  </article>

  <article style="margin-bottom: 36px;">
    <h2 style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--dusk-blue); margin-bottom: 8px;">Organizations Fail Before Technology Does</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite);">Engineering organizations don't fail because of technology. They fail because their structures, incentives, and communication patterns can't support the systems they build. Fix the organization and the technology follows.</p>
  </article>

  <article style="margin-bottom: 36px;">
    <h2 style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--dusk-blue); margin-bottom: 8px;">Progressive Influence Over Declarative Authority</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite);">Lasting change doesn't come from mandates. It comes from demonstrating value, building trust, and making the right path the easy path. Influence compounds. Authority depletes.</p>
  </article>

  <article style="margin-bottom: 36px;">
    <h2 style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--dusk-blue); margin-bottom: 8px;">Make Big Problems Small Problems</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite);">Every insurmountable challenge is a collection of tractable ones. Break things down. Find the seams. Solve the smallest meaningful piece first, then let momentum carry the rest.</p>
  </article>

  <article style="margin-bottom: 36px;">
    <h2 style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--dusk-blue); margin-bottom: 8px;">Raise the Bar, Don't Guard the Gate</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite);">Engineering excellence isn't about exclusion. It's about creating systems, patterns, and cultures that lift everyone's work. Mentor generously. Document intentionally. Build platforms that multiply capability.</p>
  </article>

  <article style="margin-bottom: 36px;">
    <h2 style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--dusk-blue); margin-bottom: 8px;">Kindness as Engineering Practice</h2>
    <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--graphite);">Being known for kindness is not weakness. Kind teams share knowledge freely, give honest feedback without cruelty, and build trust that survives hard decisions.</p>
  </article>

  <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--warm-stone); margin: 32px 0;" />

  <h2 style="font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .14em; color: var(--dusk-blue); margin-bottom: 16px;">Things I Believe</h2>
  <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px;">
    <li style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-style: italic; color: var(--mystic-purple); padding-left: 16px; border-left: 2px solid var(--dusk-blue);">Good systems leave room to evolve.</li>
    <li style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-style: italic; color: var(--mystic-purple); padding-left: 16px; border-left: 2px solid var(--dusk-blue);">The cost of complexity is cognitive, not just technical.</li>
    <li style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-style: italic; color: var(--mystic-purple); padding-left: 16px; border-left: 2px solid var(--dusk-blue);">Familiarity is not the same as fitness.</li>
    <li style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-style: italic; color: var(--mystic-purple); padding-left: 16px; border-left: 2px solid var(--dusk-blue);">Data grounds discussions. Intuition starts them.</li>
    <li style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-style: italic; color: var(--mystic-purple); padding-left: 16px; border-left: 2px solid var(--dusk-blue);">Clever code is a liability. Boring code is a gift to your future self.</li>
    <li style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-style: italic; color: var(--mystic-purple); padding-left: 16px; border-left: 2px solid var(--dusk-blue);">Don't give technical solutions to people problems.</li>
    <li style="font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif; font-style: italic; color: var(--mystic-purple); padding-left: 16px; border-left: 2px solid var(--dusk-blue);">Other folks are amazing. Be the shadow that makes their light clearer.</li>
  </ul>
</div>
